{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.QBetaBarEvenKernelTypeclass","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.QBetaBarEvenKernelTypeclass","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarEvenKernelTypeclass.barEvenKernel_nonempty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarEvenKernelTypeclass.barEvenKernel_nonempty","kind":"theorem","line":255,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-bar-even-kernel-typeclass.lean#L255-L261","doc":"The class is inhabited — the statement the three lifting lemmas rest on,\nnow available at the class rather than only in an unimported probe. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarEvenKernelTypeclass.barEvenKernelAtIntendedPoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarEvenKernelTypeclass.barEvenKernelAtIntendedPoint","kind":"def","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-bar-even-kernel-typeclass.lean#L226-L253","doc":"**`BarEvenKernel` accepts at its intended point** — `pole = u_substrate`,\n`c₂ ≡ -1`, `c₃ ≡ J_Hopf(1) = -2`, `magnitude = directionTarget`.\n\nA genuine instance, not a degenerate one: three of the four fields are\nexact equalities or a 1e-6 relative tolerance, and the parameters are the\nsubstrate values the gates were written for rather than values chosen to\npass. Together with `bar_even_kernel_reject_wrong_c2_shadow` this makes the\nclass a gate in both directions — it admits something and refuses\nsomething — which is the property the three lifting lemmas need in order to\nbe accessors rather than assumptions.\n\nA `def`, not an `instance`. It would only ever fire at these exact\narguments, so global resolution is not the hazard it is for a\nparameter-free carrier; but a caller should still say\n`letI := barEvenKernelAtIntendedPoint` and have the dependence visible at\nthe use site. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarEvenKernelTypeclass.direction_threshold_positive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarEvenKernelTypeclass.direction_threshold_positive","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-bar-even-kernel-typeclass.lean#L195-L201","doc":"**Direction threshold positivity**: 10 > 0. Used downstream when\nreasoning about the magnitude check. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarEvenKernelTypeclass.bar_even_kernel_reject_wrong_c2_shadow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarEvenKernelTypeclass.bar_even_kernel_reject_wrong_c2_shadow","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-bar-even-kernel-typeclass.lean#L175-L193","doc":"**Rejection: if any of the four invariants fail, the bundle is\nunsatisfiable.**\n\nThe Lean type system enforces this automatically — there is no\nway to construct `BarEvenKernel pole c2 c3 magnitude` if any of\nthe four field hypotheses cannot be discharged. This rejection\nlemma makes the obstruction explicit for one specific failure\nmode (wrong c_2 shadow); analogous rejection lemmas exist\nper-field in PR #1890's parametric gate classes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarEvenKernelTypeclass.barEvenKernel_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarEvenKernelTypeclass.barEvenKernel_iff","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-bar-even-kernel-typeclass.lean#L145-L173","doc":"**The bundle IS the conjunction of its gates** — the `.md`'s\n*\"instantiating `BarEvenKernel` is equivalent to clearing all four gates\nsimultaneously\"*, stated.\n\nAdded 2026-08-31 (bean `qou-z9ws`). The three lifting lemmas above are the\n**forward** half of this equivalence and nothing more: each returns the\nclass field its type restates, which is the accessor idiom\n(`Group.mul_assoc`), not a derivation. The `.md` claims an *equivalence*,\nand the converse — that the four facts suffice to build the bundle — was\nnever stated, so the block's actual claim had no Lean. It does now, and the\nlifting lemmas are one direction of it rather than free-standing\nprojections.\n\nNote that §4(b), the bar-even invariant, is deliberately **not** a field of\n`BarEvenKernel` (it is automatic for substrate-derived candidates, per the\nmodule docstring), so \"all four gates\" here is three class fields plus the\ntwo `q = 1` shadows. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarEvenKernelTypeclass.bar_even_kernel_implies_direction_sanity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarEvenKernelTypeclass.bar_even_kernel_implies_direction_sanity","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-bar-even-kernel-typeclass.lean#L133-L142","doc":"**§4(d) lifting**: from the bundle, the direction-sanity\nmagnitude-match invariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarEvenKernelTypeclass.bar_even_kernel_implies_q_one_shadow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarEvenKernelTypeclass.bar_even_kernel_implies_q_one_shadow","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-bar-even-kernel-typeclass.lean#L116-L131","doc":"**§4(c) lifting**: from the bundle, both q=1 classical-limit\nshadows hold.\n\n**Assumed, not derived here** — \"from the bundle\" means projected from\nit: the body is `⟨hK.c2_shadow, hK.c3_shadow⟩`, both conjuncts carried\nverbatim as `BarEvenKernel` fields. The lifting is the repackaging, not a\nderivation of the shadows. `c2`/`c3` are arbitrary functions, so the\nstatement is genuinely conditional and may not be strengthened to a\nglobal `axiom`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarEvenKernelTypeclass.bar_even_kernel_implies_radius_of_convergence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarEvenKernelTypeclass.bar_even_kernel_implies_radius_of_convergence","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-bar-even-kernel-typeclass.lean#L106-L114","doc":"**§4(a) lifting**: from the bundle, the radius-of-convergence\npole-location invariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarEvenKernelTypeclass.BarEvenKernel.direction_match","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarEvenKernelTypeclass.BarEvenKernel.direction_match","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-bar-even-kernel-typeclass.lean#L101-L101","doc":"§4(d) direction sanity: candidate's substrate magnitude is\nwithin the 10× threshold of the target. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarEvenKernelTypeclass.BarEvenKernel.c3_shadow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarEvenKernelTypeclass.BarEvenKernel.c3_shadow","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-bar-even-kernel-typeclass.lean#L98-L98","doc":"§4(c) q=1 classical-limit shadow for c_3: must equal\n`J_Hopf(1) = -2` (registry §3 anchor). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarEvenKernelTypeclass.BarEvenKernel.c2_shadow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarEvenKernelTypeclass.BarEvenKernel.c2_shadow","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-bar-even-kernel-typeclass.lean#L95-L95","doc":"§4(c) q=1 classical-limit shadow for c_2: must equal -1\n(PR #1786 Taylor-exact anchor). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarEvenKernelTypeclass.BarEvenKernel.pole_at_u_substrate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarEvenKernelTypeclass.BarEvenKernel.pole_at_u_substrate","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-bar-even-kernel-typeclass.lean#L91-L91","doc":"§4(a) radius-of-convergence: candidate's nearest pole is at\n`u_substrate` within the fibre-level tolerance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarEvenKernelTypeclass.BarEvenKernel.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarEvenKernelTypeclass.BarEvenKernel.mk","kind":"ctor","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-bar-even-kernel-typeclass.lean#L87-L87","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarEvenKernelTypeclass.BarEvenKernel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarEvenKernelTypeclass.BarEvenKernel","kind":"class","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-bar-even-kernel-typeclass.lean#L69-L102","doc":"**`BarEvenKernel` — the unified formalize-first typeclass.**\n\nParametric over the four candidate-specific values:\n- `pole`: the candidate's nearest singularity in the u-plane\n- `c2`, `c3`: the candidate's per-rung ladder coefficient functions\n- `magnitude`: the candidate's substrate magnitude |F(q_0)|\n\nInstantiation requires the candidate to clear all three structural\n§4 gates that depend on candidate-specific data: §4(a) radius-of-\nconvergence, §4(c) q=1 shadow, and §4(d) direction sanity. The\n§4(b) bar-even invariant is automatic for substrate-derived\ncandidates (it's a CommRing R structural identity) and is checked\nseparately via PR #1875's standalone lemma when needed.\n\nPer Gemini's HIGH-priority feedback on PR #1890: PARAMETRIC over\nthe candidate-specific arguments so multiple candidates can be\nchecked in the same environment. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:q-beta-bar-even-kernel-typeclass","label":"prop:q-beta-bar-even-kernel-typeclass","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-bar-even-kernel-typeclass.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarEvenKernelTypeclass.directionThreshold","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarEvenKernelTypeclass.directionThreshold","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-bar-even-kernel-typeclass.lean#L63-L65","doc":"Direction-sanity threshold (10× order-of-magnitude check). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarEvenKernelTypeclass.directionTarget","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarEvenKernelTypeclass.directionTarget","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-bar-even-kernel-typeclass.lean#L54-L61","doc":"Direction-sanity target magnitude (PR #1727 + PR #1786 substrate\nderivation: `Q_β / [Q_A · cos α_eff] ≈ 0.998` at q_0).\n\nComparison-boundary constant: `0.99824` is computed from the measured\n`Q_β`, so a gate stated against it is a screening check at the\ncomparison with measurement, not a derived invariant of the kernel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarEvenKernelTypeclass.jonesHopfAtQOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarEvenKernelTypeclass.jonesHopfAtQOne","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-bar-even-kernel-typeclass.lean#L50-L52","doc":"The Hopf-Jones classical value `J_Hopf(q=1) = -2` (registry §3). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarEvenKernelTypeclass.radiusTolerance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarEvenKernelTypeclass.radiusTolerance","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-bar-even-kernel-typeclass.lean#L46-L48","doc":"Radius-of-convergence fibre tolerance (1 ppm relative). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarEvenKernelTypeclass.uSubstrate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarEvenKernelTypeclass.uSubstrate","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-bar-even-kernel-typeclass.lean#L42-L44","doc":"The established u_substrate value (PR #1727 cross-anchor). ","signatureChunk":0}]}